{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas","id":1149279,"title":"How Dangerous are the Devas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-12T17:38:26-07:00","id":1149279,"title":"How Dangerous are the Devas?","content":"First of all, I am not Hindu, and I know very little about its religion beyond what I've learned through second or third hand exposure.<br /> <br /> However, it has been brought to my attention that the Devas have access to an extremely powerful armory that could be compared to modern day WMD's.<br /> <br /> Basically, you're fighting a Deva and suddenly they whip out a divine powered rocket launcher to blow your face off, or something like that.<br /> <br /> And apparently, this arsenal was the inspiration behind the <a href=\"http://naruto.wikia.com/wiki/Asura_Path\" target=\"_blank\">Rinnegan's Asura Path</a>, which turns the user's body into a military grade cyborg.<br /> <br /> So now I'm wondering just how powerful would the Devas actually be in the Scion universe, and what kind of Birthright weapons might they give out to their Scions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-12-2017, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T21:56:26-07:00","id":1149310,"title":"","content":"Hmm... the Deva's weapon panoply is considerable for two reasons: Firstly, the scale of damage they can cause - While the Astras of Indra and the other members of his court are usually described as <i>only</i> being able to destroy an army or two at once, the weapons of the Trimurti and others are often described as continent, if not outright world destroying. Part of that, I'm sure, is hyperbole... but do you really want to test that?<br /> <br /> Secondly, the sheer number of weapons available. Whereas in other Pantheons some of the most powerful and warlike deities have special weapons (The Greeks have Zeus' thunderbolt, Athena's aegis and Poseidon's trident and that's pretty much it as far as I know, not counting things like Eros' arrows which is technically a weapon but not quite the same thing) pretty much every named Deva has <i>several</i> weapons that they just keep around. Gods without a lick of Warrior like Surya or Prithvi have them. Brahma, the Creator who literally does not fight ever (except that one time he killed someone by throwing a flower at them) has <b>THREE</b> world destroying weapons to his name. Vishnu and Shiva have even more each and Durga is a walking armory.<br /> <br /> Two other more minor points... firstly, the Deva's superweapons are commonly called Astras, even in India... technically however, Astra is only the term for a <i>ranged</i> superweapon... the term for a melee superweapon is Shastra. It's just that no warrior worth his salt would be caught dead in melee in Hindu myth which considers ranged combat far more glorious and honorable (to the point where the ancient Hindu scripture on war is literally just called Dhanur Veda, 'The Knowledge of the Bow') compared to melee, so we pretty much never see the melee superweapons used and Astra has just become the generally accepted term for superweapon regardless of range of use. There's a reason the great Heroes of the Mahabharata, Arjuna and Karna, are both archers while the villain of the piece Duryodhana is a wrestler.<br /> <br /> In addition, Astras, in most interpretations, are as much spiritual as physical. While some of the most iconic ones like Vishnu's discus and Shiva's trident manifest physically, they aren't necessarily physical objects... they are spiritual weapons that are invoked and released through physical conduits. When the archers of the Mahabharata are shooting Astras at each other, they're not literally shooting special arrows around... they are invoking the power of the Astras they have received into otherwise normal arrows and shooting <i>those</i>. And since this physical conduit doesn't even have to be a traditional weapon, we have stories of people throwing around blades of grass that can split continents apart <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for how this translates over to Scion... I don't know if you've read the Scion 2e Deva Preview, but it explicitly mentions that the Deva are universally feared for their stockpile of WMDs, which no other Pantheon wants to test <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> In addition, Hindu myth is chock full of stories of the Deva giving out weapons like candy to their worshipers, so Deva Scions are likely to be well armed indeed... the Deva PSP, Yoga, explicitly has a Boon that lets you ask to borrow any Deva's Relic weapons... so go crazy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT : Sadly I am not familiar enough with Naruto to comment on the Asura Path, though Asura have sometime also gained Astras from the Deva.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T22:16:54-07:00","id":1149314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1149310#post1149310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT : Sadly I am not familiar enough with Naruto to comment on the Asura Path, though Asura have sometime also gained Astras from the Deva.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, well to summarize, there's this extremely rare power (basically achieved through spiritual enlightenment) called the Rinnegan which gives you access to 6 abilities named after the various sections of the Hindu afterlife.<br /> <br /> The Astra Path gives you the ability to transform your body parts into mechanical weapons, such as rocket launchers, flexible saws, laser cannons, est.<br /> <br /> The other 5 paths are as followers<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Deva Path</b> - Allows you to manipulate attractive and repulsive forces. Even giving you the ability to create planetoids with the aid of a gravity well.<br /> <br /> <b>Human Path</b> - Allows you to extract people's souls and read their minds.<br /> <br /> <b>Animal Path</b> - Allows you to summon and control a wide variety of powerful beasts and mythical creatures.<br /> <br /> <b>Preta Path</b> - Allows you to absorb all forms of Chakra, which can be used to cancel out other abilities which rely on it.<br /> <br /> <b>Naraka Path</b> - Allows you to summon the King of Hell in order to interrogate people, or to heal their wounds. During the interrogation process, if you lie or refuse to answer the summoner, then the King of Hell rips out your tongue and consumes it, where you'll most likely bleed to death shortly after.<br /> <br /> <b>Outer Path</b> - Allows you to control the forces of life and death","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T00:38:53-07:00","id":1149337,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty certain those six are from certain traditions of Buddhist myth, not Hindu, though obviously the two religions have a number of terms in common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T05:24:19-07:00","id":1149366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1149337#post1149337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty certain those six are from certain traditions of Buddhist myth, not Hindu, though obviously the two religions have a number of terms in common.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably true. In fact, it might have been inspired by the Buddhist afterlife, and I mixed them up by accident. Like I said, I don't have an extensive knowledge on the subject. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T06:03:04-07:00","id":1149377,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m pretty comfortable with the notion that the Deva are the strongest theopolitical* Superpower among the pantheons.<br /> <br /> *Overworld version of geopolitical","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T06:16:34-07:00","id":1149382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1149377#post1149377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m pretty comfortable with the notion that the Deva are the strongest theopolitical* Superpower among the pantheons.<br /> <br /> *Overworld version of geopolitical</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They do have <b>millions</b> of deities, after all. <br /> <br /> Basically, this equates to the Titans attempting to fight a nation who's entire population is comprised of Legend 9+ beings.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T06:33:28-07:00","id":1149388,"title":"","content":"Yeah, of all the Pantheons, I'm pretty confident consistently placing the Deva as the Superpower of all of the Pantheons. They have the numbers, several members who are functioning on a massive power scale, and the Astras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T08:11:01-07:00","id":1149415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1149388#post1149388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, of all the Pantheons, I'm pretty confident consistently placing the Deva as the Superpower of all of the Pantheons. They have the numbers, several members who are functioning on a massive power scale, and the Astras.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention being more or less the only pantheon that has had an unbroken chain of mainstream worshipers even in the real world. (Ok maybe the Shen and Kami as well, but not to the same degree.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T09:11:52-07:00","id":1149442,"title":"","content":"And for sheer number of worshippers their only competition includes a couple Levantine and middle eastern religions too busy with millenia old internecine and intranecine blood feuds and factional squabbles to likely play ball as effectively with other pantheons and right below them Buddhism who they have a strong history with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T11:36:59-07:00","id":1149482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1149415#post1149415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to mention being more or less the only pantheon that has had an unbroken chain of mainstream worshipers even in the real world. (Ok maybe the Shen and Kami as well, but not to the same degree.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In the World that isn\u2019t true though. All the pantheons have had continuous worship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T11:42:12-07:00","id":1149486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1149482#post1149482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the World that isn\u2019t true though. All the pantheons have had continuous worship.</div> </div> </div> </div>True that... though interestingly, this also implies that in the World the Deva have <i>even more</i> of a worshiper base than they do IRL, since fewer of their ancestral adherents in Asia converted to the Abrahamic religions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T12:33:01-07:00","id":1149494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1149486#post1149486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True that... though interestingly, this also implies that in the World the Deva have <i>even more</i> of a worshiper base than they do IRL, since fewer of their ancestral adherents in Asia converted to the Abrahamic religions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure it works proportionally across the board like that. Since most of the non-continuously worshipped Pantheons are in the West (+ Egypt), I think that's where there are less total Christians and Muslims* than in reality to make room for said religions.<br /> <br /> *The total Jewish population was devastated in reality in the 20th century, I think it's fair that they don't have take the hit in the World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T13:07:49-07:00","id":1149505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1149494#post1149494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not sure it works proportionally across the board like that. Since most of the non-continuously worshipped Pantheons are in the West (+ Egypt), I think that's where there are less total Christians and Muslims* than in reality to make room for said religions.<br /> <br /> *The total Jewish population was devastated in reality in the 20th century, I think it's fair that they don't have take the hit in the World.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, definitely... I don't mean to say that if, say, the population of Theoi worshipers in the World is three times as much as they are in the real world, that the number of Hindus in the World is likewise going to be three times as much as IRL... but I do expect that they, as well as Pantheons like the Shen and Kami, will have more worshipers than IRL. I am interested to know how Zoroastrianism fares in the World though... if that religion was not as overtaken by Islam in it's ancestral homeland of Iran then what caused their large scale migration to India... or are there just fewer Parsis in India since fewer felt the need to flee Iran.<br /> <br /> Given that there were notable Parsis involved in the Indian Independence Struggle, and Parsis have had a significant impact on Indian business, science and industry since then, that bit of history changing could have pretty important consequences in this part of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 10-13-2017, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T13:46:33-07:00","id":1149523,"title":"","content":"We might also say that habit of constantly flirting with death adds to the threat they pose.<br /> <br /> The Deva die all the time, only to come right back to life later on.<br /> <br /> So all of that together means you have <b>millions of deities, with access to apocalyptic weapons, and who refuse to stay down after managing to kill them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T14:58:22-07:00","id":1149548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1149482#post1149482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the World that isn\u2019t true though. All the pantheons have had continuous worship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but from what I understand of the previews, they are still minority religions for the most part. Just because people know they exist doesn't mean they follow them. But with the Deva, you have everyone that worships them without being able to actually meet them or their agents, plus some of those that wouldn't otherwise. Was the point I was getting at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T16:36:49-07:00","id":1149562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1149548#post1149548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes but from what I understand of the previews, they are still minority religions for the most part. Just because people know they exist doesn't mean they follow them. But with the Deva, you have everyone that worships them without being able to actually meet them or their agents, plus some of those that wouldn't otherwise. Was the point I was getting at.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't think I've heard of anybody in modern times still worshiping the old pantheons with any degree of significance. Like, I don't see people going around performing ritualistic human sacrifices, or seeking death in battle, or choosing mummification as a funeral arrangement. If anybody IRL still worships the old gods, they're either very secretive about it, or they're very, very rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T17:04:31-07:00","id":1149567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1149562#post1149562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think I've heard of anybody in modern times still worshiping the old pantheons with any degree of significance. Like, I don't see people going around performing ritualistic human sacrifices, or seeking death in battle, or choosing mummification as a funeral arrangement. If anybody IRL still worships the old gods, they're either very secretive about it, or they're very, very rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said they did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T17:28:07-07:00","id":1149572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1149567#post1149567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never said they did.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know. Just saying that if there are people who still follow the old religions IRL, then I've never actually heard of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T17:38:12-07:00","id":1149574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1149572#post1149572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know. Just saying that if there are people who still follow the old religions IRL, then I've never actually heard of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Tons of people follow traditional belief systems modernly, based off US Census data, there were 340,000 individuals who self-identified as 'Pagan' in the United States of America, and 186,000 who identified as following a form of First Nations religious tradition. Interestingly, both of those numbers jumped a fair bit since 2001 where those two groups sat at 140,000 and 103,000 back in 2001. People still follow such traditions, even if the details have changed over time, there are several people on the forums who do according to previous discussions on the topic. Even though these groups don't still engage in all of their traditional religious practices doesn't mean they're not still following those faiths.<br /> <br /> For example, you don't see a lot of flagellants or desert-based hermits around, but there are still Catholics. People are forced to reshape their religious practices into what a State-Entity deems appropriate behavior, for better or worse. So, modernly traditions such as animal sacrifice, and death rituals can be forcibly changed by these State-Entities by threatening legal action against the adherents of these faiths. For example, burials by exposure that we suspect some Celtic groups practiced where bodies were left out for carrion animals to consume, is illegal in Canada, and thus followers of such faiths are torn between their traditional belief, and legal action being taken against members of the community. Just because these faiths may change doesn't mean they're still not around.<br /> <br /> It might just be due to my field of study, but I have spoken with a fair number of Neo-Pagans both online, and in person. I think about eight people in person without me going to any organized ceremonies or the like. It might just be that you haven't realized some of the people who have talked to are Neo-Pagans, I don't know if it's just where I am, but people don't often come out with their religious traditions without prompting.<br /> <br /> Edit: If you are interested in becoming a member of such a community, you could probably find a local group online. With Samhain coming up for the Celtic Neo-Pagans, you might be able to attend a celebration of some sort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 10-13-2017, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T17:56:46-07:00","id":1149579,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'm aware that there are still pagans / neo-pagans walking around. But the cases I heard about usually involved Wiccans and the occasional Druid. Speaking of which, I once visited a book store that had this massive (like 4 inches thick) book that was completely dedicated to Wiccan magic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I didn't know there were still people worshiping Zeus and the like. Still, it's nice to know these theologies weren't completely eradicated by monotheism, as I find them to be quite fascinating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-13-2017, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T07:23:36-07:00","id":1149676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1149579#post1149579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't know there were still people worshiping Zeus and the like. Still, it's nice to know these theologies weren't completely eradicated by monotheism, as I find them to be quite fascinating.</div> </div> </div> </div>We exist, Nyrufa. We don't perform animal sacrifices at great festivals anymore, and for that matter if be shocked if anyone still had massive citywide celebrations for the holidays (although I acknowledge that there are likely far more followers of the religion in Greece itself rather than elsewhere, so perhaps there have been attempts that I'm unaware of). Hellenismos isn't quite as popular as the religion of the Asatru outside of its homeland, but it's still a growing reconstructionist religion, and it's followers can be as devout as the followers of any other religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T10:46:37-07:00","id":1149731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1149579#post1149579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't know there were still people worshiping Zeus and the like. Still, it's nice to know these theologies weren't completely eradicated by monotheism, as I find them to be quite fascinating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reconstructed faiths. Which are no less valid as religions, but is distinct from what\u2019s going on in \u201cthe World\u201d where there have been continuous traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T23:29:00-07:00","id":1151225,"title":"","content":"The extremely strict rules of war the Devas are supposed to follow offer their enemies some respite. Many Devas adhere to extremely strict and traditional combat conventions, like &quot;don't club a man below the belt&quot; or &quot;don't shoot a man in the back while he's fixing his chariot.&quot; You know, the kind of rules Gods and Heroes never, ever break. Especially not at the climax of a great epic when all the world is watching.<br /> <br /> One of the more widely followed rules of the rules which all the Devas follow all the time is the one about never using astras on unworthy foes. This rule is practical as well: if you miss with an astra, or you hit a target weaker than a rathi, the damage blows over into everyone and everything mortal nearby. No one wants to go down in history as the one who overestimated an enemy or mistimed a shot and then glassed Maharashtra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T13:48:11-07:00","id":1151457,"title":"","content":"Pagan adherents are not exactly ridiculously rare to the point of being unheard of, though for obvious reasons many don't walk around proclaiming their faith on their sleeves (and if they are, its possible your simply not noticing. I walk around with a clearly observable Mjolnir at all times and the amount of times I've had people ask about it because they actually recognize the symbol is dwarfed by the people thinking it looks cool).<br /> <br /> Its possible that it follows some patterns regionally, for instance your much less likely to find a pagan in some small rural town in the middle of nowhere for the same reason your less likely to find a Japanese immigrant in the same place. Extreme homogeneity breeds itself true and heterogeneity tends to attract more of the same.<br /> <br /> Under admittingly strong rules of disregarding those i would consider to be wiccans or similar (which i might add makes up the majority of adherents, so if you would like to include them you should increase this accordingly) I would say that adherents of my faith alone are populated enough in America for anyone to find a reasonably sized group of 6+ members within an hour or two of them in almost all cases, much more if your on either coast or near a large city. Its also very common in the prison system.<br /> <br /> As for the extent of current practices, I don't know any pagan groups that claim, or that i'd suspect, of performing human sacrifices. (interestingly, satanist groups, while much less common,i cannot make the same claim for). I perform animal sacrifice regularly, but its an admittingly uncommon practice to do so.<br /> <br /> Though to go on a bit of a tangent (And a possible plot source) in the US its actually much easier to get away with traditionally cultic behavior than many people actually assume do to the laws regarding freedom of worship. It is in fact legally possible to have a cult that engages in some very unsavory behavior including beating members and distributing corporal punishment, refusing to allow them to leave, sexual practices, starving adherents as punishment or restricting food for theological reasons, etc. The church of Scientology is the only group i know offhandedly that engages in this however. The Legal issues come about through rights regarding freedom of worship and also that of the informed consent of adults. For instance, If you ban a religious adherent being physically punished by priests as a part of their religious practice, then you create issues around the legality of other similar activities involving consenting adults like BDSM.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Hole_(Scientology\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Hole_(Scientology</a>) Works in just this manner (Allegedly!) with adherents having consented to the behavior beforehand including the stipulation that they not be allowed to back out of it later regardless of their pleas otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T15:26:53-07:00","id":1151493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1151457#post1151457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the extent of current practices, I don't know any pagan groups that claim, or that i'd suspect, of performing human sacrifices. (interestingly, satanist groups, while much less common,i cannot make the same claim for). I perform animal sacrifice regularly, but its an admittingly uncommon practice to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, most people have the completely wrong idea of what modern satanism is all about. It is, for lack of a better word, a religion of self worship. One of Satan's many titles is &quot;the Rebel&quot; and the satanists of today seek to emulate that. By placing your own free will above the authority of others, you become the Rebel. <b>In other words, you become Satan.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-20-2017, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T18:20:27-07:00","id":1151522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1151225#post1151225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the more widely followed rules of the rules which all the Devas follow all the time is the one about never using astras on unworthy foes. This rule is practical as well: if you miss with an astra, or you hit a target weaker than a rathi, the damage blows over into everyone and everything mortal nearby. No one wants to go down in history as the one who overestimated an enemy or mistimed a shot and then glassed Maharashtra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tunguska Event: never forget Yuri the young Slavic Scion who managed to accidentally run into Shiva on a bad day. Being cold and traveling can put anyone in a sour mood you know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T12:19:07-07:00","id":1151994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1151493#post1151493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I understand it, most people have the completely wrong idea of what modern satanism is all about. It is, for lack of a better word, a religion of self worship. One of Satan's many titles is &quot;the Rebel&quot; and the satanists of today seek to emulate that. By placing your own free will above the authority of others, you become the Rebel. <b>In other words, you become Satan.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>While that is mostly the case, there are groups that worship a Lord of Darkness. Often this is not exactly the Abrahamic Satan, but rather more Dualistic gnostic demiurge like figure that is often based on pagan deities. That is, they assume all deity like figures that could possibly be said &quot;prince of darkness&quot; actually are the same figure. Good examples of this kind of thing would be the Temple of Set and the Order of Nine Angles, along with alot of western....i'll graciously refer to them as misappropriations of Tantrik Hinduism and Vajrayana Buddhism.<br /> <br /> Basically, Alot of these are edgy teens and the like, hangers on, but it does very well exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T14:18:58-07:00","id":1152024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1151493#post1151493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I understand it, most people have the completely wrong idea of what modern satanism is all about. It is, for lack of a better word, a religion of self worship. One of Satan's many titles is &quot;the Rebel&quot; and the satanists of today seek to emulate that. By placing your own free will above the authority of others, you become the Rebel. <b>In other words, you become Satan.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately there is also a hefty amount of Randian Objectivism and Socializing Darwinism in LaVey\u2019s teachings that really needs to be understood as central to the philosophy in question.<br /> <br /> Though there are groups like the Satanic Temple (as distinct from the Church of Satan) that reject that in favor of more compassionate and egalitarian social views.<br /> <br /> I believe the Temple of Set rejects LaVeyism as well, but I am less knowledgeable of their teachings.<br /> <br /> Essentially in their respective rebellions against mainstream Christianity, the Church of Satan seeks to invert traditional Christian morality, while the Satanic Temple aligns with traditional Christian moral principles but seeks to expose what they see as Christian hypocrisy (as the politically dominant strain of conservative Chrsitianity is already said moral inversion embracing nationalism and social Darwinism - they would argue).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-22-2017, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T21:21:27-07:00","id":1152106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1149279-how-dangerous-are-the-devas?p=1151994#post1151994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While that is mostly the case, there are groups that worship a Lord of Darkness. Often this is not exactly the Abrahamic Satan, but rather more Dualistic gnostic demiurge like figure that is often based on pagan deities. That is, they assume all deity like figures that could possibly be said &quot;prince of darkness&quot; actually are the same figure. Good examples of this kind of thing would be the Temple of Set and the Order of Nine Angles, along with alot of western....i'll graciously refer to them as misappropriations of Tantrik Hinduism and Vajrayana Buddhism.<br /> <br /> Basically, Alot of these are edgy teens and the like, hangers on, but it does very well exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Tantrik myself I admit I find the idea of it being a dualistic philosophy with some sort of 'Lord of Darkness' figure almost amusingly silly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Like, I know these people are going more for 'edgy' (and, I assume, at least as far as Tantra is concerned, 'sexy') rather than accurate but Kali Krishna and Christ is that missing the point of a philosophy that at it's core is supremely monistic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Tantra is about the essential understanding that God (in whatever version you prefer though most Tantriks, like myself, are Shaktas, to the point where Shaktism and Tantra are practically synonymous at this point for a lot of people) <b>IS</b> the Universe. Therefore nothing in the universe is not Divine. Which is why historically Tantriks have ignored caste distinctions and the restrictions placed on women, and why many Tantriks indulge in ritual meat eating and sex... since those acts are considered impure by Orthodox Hindus and Tantra holds that nothing is inherently impure.<br /> <br /> Tantra also has interesting views on sin... basically, since God is All, all evil has its source in God as well as all good... so the concept of sinning <i>against</i> God, when God is all things to begin with, doesn't really compute. So Tantra by and large does not accept the concept of Sins against God, only Crimes against Humanity <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}